from (values
('127.829.d.8.A',3,'Before servicing a compressor, a technician recognizes pressurized air, a hot discharge line and a moving belt as:','["office hazards", "marketing hazards", "electrical, mechanical and thermal hazards", "weather hazards only"]'::jsonb,2,'Compressors have multiple hazards.','original'),
('127.829.d.8.A',4,'Compressed air stored in the tank must be:','["ignored", "left in place", "increased", "relieved before opening any line"]'::jsonb,3,'Release stored energy.','original'),
('127.829.d.8.B',3,'Locking out a compressor before changing the oil is meant to prevent:','["unexpected startup and release of stored energy", "a break", "a color change", "a price change"]'::jsonb,0,'LOTO protects workers.','original'),
('127.829.d.8.B',4,'For a compressor, lockout/tagout should include:','["removing tags first", "disconnecting power and bleeding off stored air pressure", "opening the tank only", "leaving it running"]'::jsonb,1,'Control all energy.','original'),
('127.829.d.8.C',3,'To disassemble a piston compressor, a technician removes the head bolts with a wrench, pulls the valve plate and slides the piston out using a ring compressor and puller. These are:','["cooking steps", "packing steps", "tools and procedures for compressor disassembly", "painting steps"]'::jsonb,2,'Disassembly uses specific tools.','original'),
('127.829.d.8.C',4,'When taking a compressor apart, a good habit is to:','["skip notes", "toss parts together", "force every part", "lay parts out in order and label them"]'::jsonb,3,'Orderly disassembly.','original'),
('127.829.d.8.D',3,'During reassembly, the technician fits new rings on the piston with the gaps staggered, installs a new head gasket and tightens bolts to specified torque. This describes:','["tools and procedures for compressor assembly", "a shipping step", "a teardown", "a cleanup"]'::jsonb,0,'Assembly follows specs.','original'),
('127.829.d.8.D',4,'The ring end gaps on a piston should be:','["lined up", "staggered around the piston", "removed", "filled with paste"]'::jsonb,1,'Staggered gaps limit leakage.','original'),
('127.829.d.8.E',3,'A technician finds a worn cylinder wall, a broken valve reed and a scored piston. She is:','["painting parts", "scrapping the unit", "inspecting the compressor to locate damage, defects and wear", "ignoring problems"]'::jsonb,2,'Inspection finds wear.','original'),
('127.829.d.8.E',4,'A compressor that loses pressure quickly may have:','["a clean filter", "a bright label", "too much paint", "worn rings or leaking valves"]'::jsonb,3,'Leaks lose pressure.','original'),
('127.829.d.8.F',3,'After reassembly, a technician starts the compressor, checks the oil pressure, listens for noise and confirms it builds pressure to the set point. She is:','["operating the newly reassembled compressor to ensure correct function", "painting the tank", "scrapping the compressor", "replacing the tank"]'::jsonb,0,'Start-up checks.','original'),
('127.829.d.8.F',4,'During first startup after a rebuild, the technician should watch for:','["paint peeling", "oil pressure, unusual noise and leaks", "tag shape", "label color"]'::jsonb,1,'Early checks catch issues.','original'),
('127.829.d.8.G',3,'A technician drains the old oil, replaces the filter, refills the sump to the proper level with the specified oil and logs it. This is:','["a painting step", "a pump repair", "proper lubrication for compressors", "a sales step"]'::jsonb,2,'Lubricate per spec.','original'),
('127.829.d.8.G',4,'Compressor oil should be changed:','["only when the sump is empty", "never", "whenever convenient", "according to the manufacturer''s schedule"]'::jsonb,3,'Follow the schedule.','original'),
('127.829.d.8.H',3,'After rebuilding a compressor, a technician enters the ring kit part number, date and run hours into the shop''s maintenance system. This is:','["recording information about parts and materials used", "hiding the repair", "erasing history", "tossing records"]'::jsonb,0,'Record keeping.','original'),
('127.829.d.8.H',4,'A computer record of repairs on a compressor helps a maintenance team to:','["increase repairs", "plan future service and spot repeat failures", "avoid planning", "hide failures"]'::jsonb,1,'History reveals patterns.','original'),
('127.829.d.9.A',3,'On a teardown bench, a trainee points to the rubber lip seal around a compressor shaft and the curved blades inside a centrifugal pump. She is identifying:','["motor windings", "drive belts", "internal seals and vanes", "pipe labels"]'::jsonb,2,'Seals contain fluid; vanes move it.','original'),
('127.829.d.9.A',4,'Which pair correctly matches a part to its job inside a pump?','["a seal moves the fluid; a vane keeps it contained", "both only support the shaft", "both only decorate", "a vane moves the fluid; a seal keeps the fluid contained"]'::jsonb,3,'Vanes move, seals contain.','original'),
('127.829.d.9.B',3,'A technician holds an impeller to the light and checks each vane for cracks, thinning and chipped edges. She is inspecting:','["vanes in a centrifugal pump for wear and damage", "hoses on a tank", "bearings in a motor", "belts on a drive"]'::jsonb,0,'Vane inspection.','original'),
('127.829.d.9.B',4,'Eroded, thinned vanes on an impeller usually cause the pump to:','["produce more pressure", "lose flow and efficiency", "run quieter and stronger", "gain flow"]'::jsonb,1,'Worn vanes reduce output.','original'),
('127.829.d.9.C',3,'A technician looks at a mechanical seal''s carbon face and finds it grooved and cracked. She is inspecting:','["motors for color", "belts for tension", "internal seals for wear and damage", "gears for noise"]'::jsonb,2,'Inspect seal faces.','original'),
('127.829.d.9.C',4,'An internal seal that shows scoring on its face should be:','["painted", "left in place", "reused", "replaced"]'::jsonb,3,'Damaged seals leak.','original'),
('127.829.d.9.D',3,'Pulling the cover off a diaphragm pump, a technician flexes the rubber membrane and looks for cracks, holes and hardening. She is:','["inspecting the diaphragm for damage, defects and wear", "testing a motor", "tuning a belt", "fixing a gauge"]'::jsonb,0,'Diaphragm inspection.','original'),
('127.829.d.9.D',4,'A diaphragm that looks stretched and cracked near its center should be:','["painted", "replaced before it ruptures", "reused for another year", "ignored"]'::jsonb,1,'Cracks lead to failure.','original'),
('127.829.d.9.E',3,'Looking at a pump''s housing, a technician locates the ball bearings that support the shaft at each end. She is:','["identifying vanes", "identifying gauges", "identifying bearings on a pump", "identifying seals"]'::jsonb,2,'Bearings support shafts.','original'),
('127.829.d.9.E',4,'The two bearings on a pump shaft are typically housed:','["inside the impeller", "outside the base", "in the motor fan", "at each end of the shaft in the bearing housing"]'::jsonb,3,'Bearings sit at shaft ends.','original'),
('127.829.d.9.F',3,'A technician spins a bearing by hand and feels roughness and hears grinding. She is inspecting:','["bearings on pumps and compressors for damage and wear", "gears for color", "hoses for length", "belts for price"]'::jsonb,0,'Rough spinning means wear.','original'),
('127.829.d.9.F',4,'A bearing with blue discoloration on the races most likely has:','["been refrigerated", "been overheated", "been polished", "been over-greased only"]'::jsonb,1,'Blue color shows heat damage.','original'),
('127.829.d.10.A',3,'Why does a compressor shaft have a seal where it exits the housing?','["to cool the motor", "to make the shaft turn faster", "to keep oil or air from leaking out and contaminants from getting in", "to change the color"]'::jsonb,2,'Seals contain and exclude.','original'),
('127.829.d.10.A',4,'Without good internal seals, a pump would lose:','["weight", "color", "only labels", "pressure and fluid"]'::jsonb,3,'Leaks lower performance.','original'),
('127.829.d.10.B',3,'Bearings in a pump and compressor are used to:','["support the rotating shaft and reduce friction", "stop the shaft", "add friction", "change the voltage"]'::jsonb,0,'Bearings reduce friction.','original'),
('127.829.d.10.B',4,'A ball bearing reduces friction by:','["using paint", "letting balls roll between the inner and outer races", "sliding metal on metal dry", "adding weight"]'::jsonb,1,'Rolling elements reduce friction.','original'),
('127.829.d.10.C',3,'A diaphragm pump uses two small valves that open to let fluid in and close to keep it from flowing backward as the membrane moves. These are:','["globe valves", "relief valves", "check valves", "gate valves"]'::jsonb,2,'Check valves control direction.','original'),
('127.829.d.10.C',4,'In a diaphragm pump, the suction check valve opens during the:','["discharge stroke", "off cycle only", "cleaning cycle", "intake stroke, letting fluid enter the chamber"]'::jsonb,3,'Suction check opens on intake.','original'),
('127.829.d.10.D',3,'A maintenance manual lists the oil type, the oil level and a change interval for a compressor. These are:','["lubrication requirements", "wiring needs", "shipping needs", "paint needs"]'::jsonb,0,'Follow lubrication specs.','original'),
('127.829.d.10.D',4,'A pump bearing that is lubricated too little will most likely:','["run cooler", "overheat and wear out early", "never fail", "last longer"]'::jsonb,1,'Lack of lubrication causes failure.','original'),
('127.829.d.11.A',3,'Two parallel-shaft gears have straight teeth cut parallel to the axis. They are:','["bevel gears", "helical gears", "spur gears", "worm gears"]'::jsonb,2,'Spur gears have straight teeth.','original'),
('127.829.d.11.A',4,'A spur gear drive is commonly used to:','["connect shafts at 90 degrees", "pump fluid", "cool oil", "transmit power between parallel shafts"]'::jsonb,3,'Spur gears link parallel shafts.','original'),
('127.829.d.11.B',3,'A pair of gears with angled teeth that mesh gradually and run quietly are:','["helical gears", "slinger gears", "miter gears", "spur gears"]'::jsonb,0,'Helical teeth are angled.','original'),
('127.829.d.11.B',4,'A benefit of helical gears over spur gears is that they:','["produce no axial thrust", "run more smoothly and quietly", "need no lubrication", "are always cheaper"]'::jsonb,1,'Gradual engagement.','original'),
('127.829.d.11.C',3,'Gears with cone-shaped surfaces that change the direction of power by 90 degrees are:','["spur gears", "helical gears", "bevel and miter gears", "rack gears"]'::jsonb,2,'Bevel/miter gears turn power.','original'),
('127.829.d.11.C',4,'A mechanical drive that must change the shaft direction by a right angle would use:','["a hammer", "spur gears", "belts only", "bevel or miter gears"]'::jsonb,3,'Right-angle drives.','original'),
('127.829.d.11.D',3,'Two bevel gears of the same size and number of teeth that connect shafts at 90 degrees with a 1:1 ratio are called:','["miter gears", "worm gears", "helical gears", "spur gears"]'::jsonb,0,'Miters have equal teeth.','original'),
('127.829.d.11.D',4,'Compared with miter gears, bevel gears may:','["be flat", "have different numbers of teeth and change speed", "always have equal teeth", "never mesh"]'::jsonb,1,'Bevel gears can have different tooth counts.','original'),
('127.829.d.11.E',3,'A small disc on a shaft dips into the oil in the gearbox and flings oil to the bearings as it turns. This part is called a:','["coupling", "seal", "slinger", "vane"]'::jsonb,2,'Slingers distribute oil.','original'),
('127.829.d.11.E',4,'Slingers are used on gearboxes to:','["add heat", "stop the shaft", "reduce oil", "distribute lubricant to parts that are not submerged"]'::jsonb,3,'Spread oil.','original'),
('127.829.d.12.A',3,'To remove a V-belt from a drive, a technician loosens the motor mounting bolts, slides the motor toward the driven shaft, and slips the belt off without prying it. This is:','["a procedure used for disassembling a belt drive", "a shipping step", "a painting step", "a pricing step"]'::jsonb,0,'Relieve tension first.','original'),
('127.829.d.12.A',4,'Prying a belt over a sheave with a screwdriver can:','["improve the fit", "damage the belt and sheave and cause injury", "have no effect", "extend belt life"]'::jsonb,1,'Don''t pry belts.','original'),
('127.829.d.12.B',3,'A technician working near a belt and chain drive knows hair, loose clothing and fingers can be caught in the pinch point. This is a:','["parking issue", "marketing issue", "safety hazard of assembling and disassembling drives", "accounting issue"]'::jsonb,2,'Pinch points cause injuries.','original'),
('127.829.d.12.B',4,'Before working on a chain drive, the technician should:','["remove guards while running", "run the machine", "hold the chain", "lock out the power and block the shaft from turning"]'::jsonb,3,'Control energy.','original'),
('127.829.d.13.A',3,'A technician reads the number on the side of a belt, measures its width and checks the sheave groove to select a replacement. She is identifying:','["belt style, size and application", "chain sizes", "bolt colors", "pump sizes"]'::jsonb,0,'Match belt to drive.','original'),
('127.829.d.13.A',4,'A V-belt marked ''B'' means it has a:','["specific weight", "specific cross-section width and depth", "specific color", "specific price"]'::jsonb,1,'Letters indicate cross-section.','original'),
('127.829.d.13.B',3,'For a B-section belt drive, the technician chooses a sheave with grooves made for B-section belts. She is:','["picking a chain", "picking a pump", "identifying the proper sheave for the belt application", "picking a bolt"]'::jsonb,2,'Match sheave to belt.','original'),
('127.829.d.13.B',4,'A belt that rides too deep or too high in a sheave groove likely indicates:','["new equipment", "perfect fit", "low noise", "the wrong belt or worn sheave"]'::jsonb,3,'Wrong match or wear.','original'),
('127.829.d.13.C',3,'In a belt drive, the sheave on the motor shaft that delivers power is the:','["drive sheave", "driven sheave", "idler only", "bearing"]'::jsonb,0,'The drive sheave is on the motor.','original')
