('127.829.d.13.C',4,'The sheave on the fan shaft that receives power from the belt is the:','["motor", "driven sheave", "gearbox", "drive sheave"]'::jsonb,1,'The driven sheave is on the load.','original'),
('127.829.d.13.D',3,'A 4-inch drive sheave turns a 8-inch driven sheave. The speed ratio is:','["1:2 and runs faster", "4:1 and runs faster", "2:1, so the driven sheave runs at half the drive speed", "1:1"]'::jsonb,2,'8 ÷ 4 = 2.','original'),
('127.829.d.13.D',4,'A motor turns at 1,750 rpm with a 5-inch sheave. To get the driven shaft to turn at about 875 rpm, the driven sheave should be:','["20 inches", "2.5 inches", "5 inches", "10 inches"]'::jsonb,3,'1750 × 5 ÷ 875 = 10.','original'),
('127.829.d.13.E',3,'A technician finds cracks on a V-belt and a shiny, worn groove in a sheave. She is inspecting:','["a sheave and belt for wear and possible replacement", "a pump for noise", "a valve for flow", "a seal for leaks"]'::jsonb,0,'Inspect belts and sheaves.','original'),
('127.829.d.13.E',4,'A belt that is glazed, cracked or frayed should be:','["tightened more", "replaced", "painted", "reused"]'::jsonb,1,'Worn belts fail.','original'),
('127.829.d.13.F',3,'A technician counts the roller chain''s pitch and checks that it fits the sprocket teeth. She is:','["choosing a belt", "choosing a pump", "identifying chain size to match the sprocket", "choosing a gear oil"]'::jsonb,2,'Chain pitch must match.','original'),
('127.829.d.13.F',4,'A #40 roller chain has a pitch of:','["3/8 inch", "1/4 inch", "1 inch", "1/2 inch"]'::jsonb,3,'#40 = 4/8 inch.','original'),
('127.829.d.13.G',3,'A 12-tooth drive sprocket drives a 36-tooth sprocket. The driven sprocket turns:','["one third as fast", "the same speed", "three times faster", "twice as fast"]'::jsonb,0,'36 ÷ 12 = 3.','original'),
('127.829.d.13.G',4,'To double the output speed of a chain drive, the driven sprocket should have:','["twice as many teeth", "half as many teeth as the drive sprocket", "the same teeth", "no teeth"]'::jsonb,1,'Smaller driven = faster.','original'),
('127.829.d.13.H',3,'A technician uses a chain breaker tool to push out a pin and shorten a roller chain to the right length. She is:','["cutting with a torch", "bending the chain", "adjusting chain length by breaking roller chain with a special tool", "cleaning the chain"]'::jsonb,2,'Chain breakers remove pins.','original'),
('127.829.d.13.H',4,'Why use a chain breaker rather than a torch to shorten a roller chain?','["a torch is cheaper", "a torch is safer", "a torch is cooler", "a torch can damage the chain''s hardened parts"]'::jsonb,3,'Heat weakens the chain.','original'),
('127.829.d.13.I',3,'After breaking the chain to length, the technician installs a master link with the clip facing against the direction of travel. She is:','["assembling a chain according to length and sprocket spacing", "painting a chain", "testing a chain", "disassembling a chain"]'::jsonb,0,'Assemble correctly.','original'),
('127.829.d.13.I',4,'A master link clip should be installed with:','["the clip off", "its closed end facing the direction of travel", "its open end forward", "random orientation"]'::jsonb,1,'Clip orientation prevents loss.','original'),
('127.829.d.13.J',3,'A technician checks a chain for stretch with a ruler and examines sprocket teeth for hooked profiles. She is:','["setting a belt", "adjusting a seal", "inspecting sprocket and chain for wear and possible replacement", "cleaning a shaft"]'::jsonb,2,'Chain stretch and tooth wear.','original'),
('127.829.d.13.J',4,'A chain stretched more than about 3% of its length should be:','["lubricated only", "painted", "reused", "replaced along with a worn sprocket if needed"]'::jsonb,3,'Stretch beyond limits means replace.','original'),
('127.829.d.14.A',3,'A student learns about jobs as an industrial maintenance technician, millwright and machinery mechanic. These are examples of:','["special skill career pathways in manufacturing", "restaurant jobs", "retail jobs", "teaching jobs only"]'::jsonb,0,'Career pathways.','original'),
('127.829.d.14.A',4,'A technician who keeps pumps, compressors and drives running in a factory works in the career pathway of:','["culinary arts", "industrial maintenance", "education", "fashion design"]'::jsonb,1,'Maintenance pathway.','original'),
('127.829.d.14.B',3,'A student attends a local maintenance trade association meeting and talks with technicians about job openings. This shows the importance of:','["avoiding professionals", "staying isolated", "industry networking opportunities", "skipping events"]'::jsonb,2,'Networking helps careers.','original'),
('127.829.d.14.B',4,'One benefit of joining a professional organization is that members can:','["lose contacts", "avoid new skills", "reduce pay", "learn about training, certifications and jobs"]'::jsonb,3,'Organizations provide resources.','original'),
('127.829.d.14.C',3,'A technician troubleshoots a failing compressor, replaces its bearing and logs the repair for the next shift. This describes the:','["roles and functions of an industrial maintenance technician", "duties of a bank teller", "job of a chef", "role of an actor"]'::jsonb,0,'Technicians repair and document.','original'),
('127.829.d.14.C',4,'A key function of an industrial maintenance technician is to:','["design clothing", "keep equipment safe, reliable and running", "cook meals", "sell cars"]'::jsonb,1,'Maintenance keeps production going.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
